{
  "id": "al8",
  "title": "Flags and Decisions",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "al8-l1",
      "title": "The Zero Flag",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "After most arithmetic, the 8080 sets flags: little one-bit notes about the result. The zero flag (Z) is set when the result is 0.",
        "JZ (312) jumps only if the zero flag is set; JNZ (302) jumps only if it isn't. Every other time, the program just continues.",
        "DCR, INR, ADD, SUB and their friends set the flags. MOV and MVI don't."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "003   ;      3",
          "326   ; 002: SUI",
          "003   ;      3",
          "312   ; 004: JZ zero",
          "014   ;      address 014 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "076   ; 007: MVI A",
          "001   ;      1",
          "323   ; 011: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 013: HLT",
          "076   ; 014: MVI A   ← zero",
          "377   ;      255",
          "323   ; 016: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 020: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ●●●●●●●● = 255"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al8-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "When is the zero flag set?",
          "options": [
            "When a result is 0",
            "When A is 255",
            "After every MOV",
            "When the program starts"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Z = the result was Zero."
        },
        {
          "id": "al8-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does JNZ do?",
          "options": [
            "Jumps if the result was not zero",
            "Jumps if it was zero",
            "Always jumps",
            "Stops"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Jump if Not Zero."
        },
        {
