    {
      "id": "al8-l2",
      "title": "CPI and the Carry",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "CPI n (376) compares A with n: it subtracts, sets the flags, and throws the result away. A stays the same.",
        "If A equals n, the zero flag is set. If A is smaller than n, the subtraction needs a borrow, so the carry flag is set.",
        "JC (332) jumps if the carry is set, JNC (322) if it isn't. So CPI 10 then JC means: jump if A < 10."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "007   ;      7",
          "376   ; 002: CPI",
          "012   ;      10",
          "332   ; 004: JC small",
          "014   ;      address 014 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "076   ; 007: MVI A",
          "000   ;      0",
          "323   ; 011: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 013: HLT",
          "076   ; 014: MVI A   ← small",
          "001   ;      1",
          "323   ; 016: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 020: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○○○○● = 1"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al8-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does CPI 20 do to A?",
          "options": [
            "Nothing: it only sets the flags",
            "Subtracts 20",
            "Sets A to 20",
            "Adds 20"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "ComPare Immediate."
        },
        {
          "id": "al8-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "After CPI 20, when is the carry set?",
          "options": [
            "When A is smaller than 20",
            "When A equals 20",
            "When A is bigger",
            "Never"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "A - 20 needs a borrow."
        },
        {
          "id": "al8-l2-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "After CPI 20, when is the zero flag set?",
          "options": [
            "When A equals 20",
            "When A is 0",
            "When A is smaller",
            "Always"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "A - 20 = 0."
        },
        {
          "id": "al8-l2-e4",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "Set the switches to CPI (3 7 6).",
          "answer": 254,
          "explanation": "11 111 110."
        },
        {
          "id": "al8-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What do the lights show?",
          "code": [
            "076   ; 000: MVI A",
            "062   ;      50",
            "376   ; 002: CPI",
            "012   ;      10",
            "332   ; 004: JC small",
            "014   ;      address 014 (low byte)",
            "000   ;      (high byte)",
            "076   ; 007: MVI A",
            "000   ;      0",
            "323   ; 011: OUT 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "166   ; 013: HLT",
            "076   ; 014: MVI A   ← small",
            "001   ;      1",
            "323   ; 016: OUT 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "166   ; 020: HLT"
          ],
          "options": [
            "0",
            "1",
            "50",
            "10"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "50 isn't smaller than 10, so JC doesn't jump: A becomes 0."
        },
        {
          "id": "al8-l2-e6",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Jump if A was not smaller (no carry).",
