    },
    {
      "id": "al8-l3",
      "title": "Choosing the Bigger One",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "With CMP r (2 7 r), A is compared with a register instead of a number. CMP B then JNC: A is at least as big as B.",
        "Decisions on the 8080 always look like this: compare, then a conditional jump around the code you want to skip.",
        "Many jumps that skip each other make a program hard to follow. Draw arrows on the listing, like programmers did on paper."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "072   ; 000: LDA x",
          "017   ;      address 017 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "107   ; 003: MOV B,A",
          "072   ; 004: LDA y",
          "020   ;      address 020 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "270   ; 007: CMP B",
          "322   ; 010: JNC show",
          "014   ;      address 014 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "170   ; 013: MOV A,B",
          "323   ; 014: OUT 377   ← show",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 016: HLT",
          "052   ; 017: data: 42",
          "021   ; 020: data: 17"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○●○●○●○ = 42"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al8-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does CMP B do?",
          "options": [
            "Compares A with B and sets the flags",
            "Copies B",
            "Adds B",
            "Swaps A and B"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Like CPI, but with a register."
        },
        {
          "id": "al8-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "After CMP B, the carry is not set. What do you know?",
          "options": [
            "A is at least as big as B",
            "A is smaller than B",
            "A equals B",
            "Nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "No borrow was needed."
        },
        {
          "id": "al8-l3-e3",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "Set the switches to CMP C (2 7 1).",
          "answer": 185,
          "explanation": "10 111 001."
        },
        {
          "id": "al8-l3-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "In the example, why does MOV A,B come after JNC?",
          "options": [
            "If A is smaller, the bigger value is in B",
            "It always runs",
            "To show B",
            "CMP needs it"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "When JNC doesn't jump, B is bigger, so it's copied into A."
        },
        {
          "id": "al8-l3-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What do the lights show?",
          "code": [
            "006   ; 000: MVI B",
            "011   ;      9",
            "076   ; 002: MVI A",
            "004   ;      4",
            "270   ; 004: CMP B",
            "322   ; 005: JNC show",
            "011   ;      address 011 (low byte)",
            "000   ;      (high byte)",
            "170   ; 010: MOV A,B",
            "323   ; 011: OUT 377   ← show",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "166   ; 013: HLT"
          ],
          "options": [
            "9",
